{"opening": "I am a student studying in the University of Hong Kong. I must choose my courses before the deadline. All of my courses were gone in one evening. What happened?", "reference_answer": "I needed to attend a mandatory high table dinner and was asked to indicate which courses I prefer to eat before the deadline. In the evening when I attended the high table dinner, I arrived punctually. I did not finish every course in my three-course meal because I don't like its taste. Therefore I asked the waiter to collect the remains each time he serves the next course and thus my courses are eventually gone.", "story_context": {"puzzle_id": "TS013", "opening": "I am a student studying in the University of Hong Kong. I must choose my courses before the deadline. All of my courses were gone in one evening. What happened?", "reference_answer": "I needed to attend a mandatory high table dinner and was asked to indicate which courses I prefer to eat before the deadline. In the evening when I attended the high table dinner, I arrived punctually. I did not finish every course in my three-course meal because I don't like its taste. Therefore I asked the waiter to collect the remains each time he serves the next course and thus my courses are eventually gone.", "canonical_solution": "I needed to attend a mandatory high table dinner and was asked to indicate which courses I prefer to eat before the deadline. In the evening when I attended the high table dinner, I arrived punctually. I did not finish every course in my three-course meal because I don't like its taste. Therefore I asked the waiter to collect the remains each time he serves the next course and thus my courses are eventually gone.

The narrator successfully booked the dinner choices and received confirmation of that dinner allocation; this is not academic enrolment. Dishes are served as individual portions. The narrator tastes each dish before asking for the disliked leftovers to be removed, and does not leave before all courses are served. Removed dishes do not reappear.", "canonical_facts": ["Courses means dishes at a mandatory high-table dinner, not academic classes", "The deadline is for meal preferences", "The student attends on time but dislikes the food and leaves portions of the three-course meal", "At the student’s request the waiter clears leftovers when serving each next dish, so all courses disappear", "The narrator successfully booked the dinner choices and received confirmation of that dinner allocation; this is not academic enrolment. Dishes are served as individual portions. The narrator tastes each dish before asking for the disliked leftovers to be removed, and does not leave before all courses are served. Removed dishes do not reappear."], "explicit_negatives": ["An action or mistake in an academic course-selection/enrolment system did not cause the courses to disappear.", "The narrator did not finish all the food; the disappearance is not caused by all dishes being eaten by the narrator or by other attendees.", "No academic registration operation, administrative purge, wrong order, cancelled event, absence or late arrival causes the disappearance.", "The narrator does not misunderstand the meaning of the word courses; the opening misdirects the reader."], "unknown_details": ["The exact time interval between indicating meal preferences and attending the dinner, or between submitting preferences and dishes being cleared, is unspecified."], "irrelevant_details": [], "completion_requirements": ["Courses means dishes at a mandatory high-table dinner, not academic classes", "The deadline is for meal preferences", "The student attends on time but dislikes the food and leaves portions of the three-course meal", "At the student’s request the waiter clears leftovers when serving each next dish, so all courses disappear"], "event_order": ["Before the deadline the narrator indicates meal preferences and books attendance.", "The narrator arrives punctually at the mandatory high-table dinner.", "The narrator tastes a course, dislikes its taste, and leaves an uneaten portion.", "At the narrator’s request a waiter clears those leftovers when serving the next course; the repeated clearing explains why all courses are gone."], "knowledge_states": [], "label_boundaries": ["Reject academic course-selection-system causation with no, even when the question contains the true fragment that the narrator performed an own action. The actual causal action was asking the waiter to clear disliked meal leftovers; a question only asserting that waiter request is yes. Confirmed dinner booking must not be interpreted as academic registration or as the disappearance mechanism.", "A broad question asking whether the narrator’s own action caused the disappearance is yes: asking the waiter to clear leftovers is that action. Parenthetical such-as examples of accidental deletion do not restrict this broad existential question. A question explicitly claiming an action IN an academic selection system, or BY deleting enrolments, is no.", "Eating, tasting, or consuming some of each meal course is yes. Finishing all dishes or attributing disappearance to eating everything is no. A correct course/food pun alone is not the complete causal explanation.", "A broad other-person-taking-away question is yes because the waiter clears leftovers. Inclusive OR with a true removal branch is yes; it does not confirm that dishes were served to a different diner. Wrong-table delivery or other people eating the narrator’s food is no.", "A claim that staff cleared a dish before the narrator could taste it is no; the narrator tasted it before requesting removal. Asking merely about staff clearing leftovers is yes.", "The interval shortly before is unspecified incidental timing: a question focused on that interval is irrelevant. Do not turn confirmed booking into a new immediately preceding submission event."], "reference_library": {"eafbb163c52b983a": {"question": "Is this statement correct: Courses means dishes at a mandatory high-table dinner, not academic classes?", "answer": "yes"}, "353e4a6b52ff0914": {"question": "Is this statement false: Courses means dishes at a mandatory high-table dinner, not academic classes?", "answer": "no"}, "f94d9a5229e15fd3": {"question": "Were the dishes taken away because you could not attend the dinner?", "answer": "no"}}, "active_example_ids": ["eafbb163c52b983a", "353e4a6b52ff0914", "f94d9a5229e15fd3"]}, "rubric": [{"id": "C1", "weight": 0.5, "core": true, "criterion": "Courses refers to meal courses at a formal high-table dinner, not academic classes.", "full_credit": "Courses refers to meal courses at a formal high-table dinner, not academic classes.", "half_credit": "Meal rather than academic courses identified without dinner setting", "zero_credit": "Missing, contradicted, only repeats the opening without the required explanation, or gives uncommitted incompatible guesses.", "points": 50.0, "required_facts": ["Courses refers to meal courses at a formal high-table dinner, not academic classes."], "coverage_note": "Assess every qualifier; covered requires the entire fact. Partial factual coverage cannot receive full credit."}, {"id": "C2", "weight": 0.3, "core": false, "criterion": "The deadline was for expressing meal-course preferences.", "full_credit": "The deadline was for expressing meal-course preferences.", "half_credit": "Meal choice identified without deadline connection", "zero_credit": "Missing, contradicted, only repeats the opening without the required explanation, or gives uncommitted incompatible guesses.", "points": 30.0, "required_facts": ["The deadline was for expressing meal-course preferences."], "coverage_note": "Assess every qualifier; covered requires the entire fact. Partial factual coverage cannot receive full credit."}, {"id": "C3", "weight": 0.2, "core": false, "criterion": "The waiter clears uneaten dishes, making all the courses disappear.", "full_credit": "The waiter clears uneaten dishes, making all the courses disappear.", "half_credit": "Dishes disappearing identified but waiter clearing leftovers omitted", "zero_credit": "Missing, contradicted, only repeats the opening without the required explanation, or gives uncommitted incompatible guesses.", "points": 20.0, "required_facts": ["The waiter clears uneaten dishes, making all the courses disappear."], "coverage_note": "Assess every qualifier; covered requires the entire fact. Partial factual coverage cannot receive full credit."}], "completion_requirements": ["Courses means dishes at a mandatory high-table dinner, not academic classes", "The deadline is for meal preferences", "The student attends on time but dislikes the food and leaves portions of the three-course meal", "At the student’s request the waiter clears leftovers when serving each next dish, so all courses disappear"], "grading_notes": "AI three-review adjudication v2, pending human confirmation. Score only this submission. Apply full_credit/half_credit/zero_credit explicitly, with zero taking precedence for a materially contradictory checkpoint claim. An omitted qualifier can be partial; replacing the core identity/cause with a wrong one is not an omission. Faithful paraphrases count. Partial score and full narrative are separate outputs. AI independent review B, pending human approval. Credit is 0/.5/1 per checkpoint. Full narrative additionally requires all sourced completion requirements and no incompatible central claims. Judge the submitted explanation, not unasserted chat guesses. Accept faithful paraphrases; missing optional detail is not a contradiction. Do not demand unknown motives, devices or events. Accept faithful paraphrase. Require the listed identities, events and causal links, not exact prose or unspecified incidental details.", "submitted_explanation": "The opening is a wordplay trap. "Courses" and the "deadline" do not refer to academic modules and course registration at all; they refer to the dishes (courses of a meal) that the student had to choose in advance for a university hall/high-table dinner. She is a student at HKU and did make her menu choices by the dinner deadline, but the puzzle is about the meal, not her degree.

At the formal hall dinner, the dishes she had chosen were served to her, but she managed only to taste a small portion of each one. Her plates were then cleared by the waiting staff before she had finished, and the unfinished food was taken away and thrown out rather than kept for her. Because the dishes had been removed and discarded, by the end of the evening all the courses she had chosen were "gone," leaving her without a full dinner even though nothing supernatural or academic had happened.", "grading_protocol": "coverage-v2", "required_facts": [{"id": "C1.F1", "checkpoint_id": "C1", "fact": "Courses refers to meal courses at a formal high-table dinner, not academic classes."}, {"id": "C2.F1", "checkpoint_id": "C2", "fact": "The deadline was for expressing meal-course preferences."}, {"id": "C3.F1", "checkpoint_id": "C3", "fact": "The waiter clears uneaten dishes, making all the courses disappear."}], "required_completion": [{"id": "R1", "fact": "Courses means dishes at a mandatory high-table dinner, not academic classes"}, {"id": "R2", "fact": "The deadline is for meal preferences"}, {"id": "R3", "fact": "The student attends on time but dislikes the food and leaves portions of the three-course meal"}, {"id": "R4", "fact": "At the student’s request the waiter clears leftovers when serving each next dish, so all courses disappear"}]}

